p.src:
Proof. Let $L(t)$ denote cumulative loss from the onset of the outage, and normalize $L(0)=0$. During the period in which the funds transfer system is down, we idealize the loss process by $\begin{aligned}
\frac{dL}{dt} &= r, \qquad F=\text{down},\\
L(\Delta t)-L(0) &= \int_{0}^{\Delta t} r\,dt = r\,\Delta t.\end{aligned}$ Hence $L(\Delta t)=r\,\Delta t$. ◻

